<title>USA: PG&amp;E Calif. nuke cuts power for repairs.</title>
<headline>PG&amp;E Calif. nuke cuts power for repairs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pacific Gas and Electric Co's 1,087 megawatt Diablo Canyon nuclear power unit 1 cut output to 50 percent of capacity over the weekend for repairs, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>Power at the Avila Beach, Calif., unit was reduced for condenser cleaning, the NRC said in its daily plant status report.</p>
<p>A company spokesman was not immediately available to comment on when the plant would return to full power.</p>
<p>The 1,073 megawatt Diablo Canyon nuclear unit 2 was operating at full capacity, the NRC said in the status report.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
</text>
